# Test: a unit's RA rdnss dns-source is refused at ze config validate when it
#       names a class the consumer refuses, or two sources and no mode
# VALIDATES: spec-home-cpe-23b AC-11 and AC-16b, the RA rdnss consumer (the
#            other consumers are test/parse/dns-source-class-refused.ci
#            and test/parse/dns-source-mode-required-consumers.ci):
#              seq=1  a unit's RA rdnss dns-source source radius (AC-11)
#              seq=2  a unit's RA rdnss dns-source with two sources and no
#                     mode (AC-16b)
#            seq 1 is dnssource.NewWrittenList with raRDNSSRefusals, seq 2 is
#            dnssource.NewList's ModeRequiredError, both reached through
#            iface's RA reader.
# PREVENTS: an RDNSS list naming a subscriber's RADIUS resolvers, or one whose
#           sources Ze would have to guess are a backup or an addition,
#           passing validate.
# PLATFORM: the ipv6 container carries ze:os "linux", so the schema walker
#           prunes it on other platforms. This test is linux-only.
# Break: tmp/session/2026-11-07-104251/scratch/rwinv/c23b-class-refusal-ignored
#        (NewWrittenList never matches a refused class): seq 1 goes red.
#        tmp/session/2026-11-07-104251/scratch/rwinv/c23b-mode-unchecked
#        (NewList never asks for a mode): seq 2 goes red.
#        Observed in rwinv/out-gb17/ on Ze's guest: clean pass (b17-ra-clean.log),
#        "seq 1: expected exit code 1, got 0" under the class break
#        (b17-ra-class.log), "seq 2: expected exit code 1, got 0" under the
#        mode break (b17-ra-mode.log).
option=skip-os:value=darwin

stdin=ra-radius:terminator=EOF_RA_RADIUS
interface {
	backend netlink;
	ethernet eth0 {
		unit 0 {
			ipv6 {
				address [ 2001:db8:1::1/64 ];
				forwarding true;
				router-advertisement {
					enabled true;
					rdnss {
						dns-source {
							source radius;
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_RA_RADIUS

stdin=ra-no-mode:terminator=EOF_RA_NO_MODE
interface {
	backend netlink;
	ethernet eth0 {
		unit 0 {
			ipv6 {
				address [ 2001:db8:1::1/64 ];
				forwarding true;
				router-advertisement {
					enabled true;
					rdnss {
						dns-source {
							source [ received configured ];
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_RA_NO_MODE

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=ra-radius:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=interface ethernet eth0 unit 0 ipv6 router-advertisement rdnss dns-source names radius
expect=stdout:contains=a host on this link is not a subscriber
expect=stdout:contains=delete interface ethernet eth0 unit 0 ipv6 router-advertisement rdnss dns-source source radius

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=ra-no-mode:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=interface ethernet eth0 unit 0 ipv6 router-advertisement rdnss dns-source names 2 sources (received, configured) and no mode
